mdgen/mdlint on GNU tools
=========================

    make mdtools TOOLCHAIN=gnu

Builds from src/hypervisor/src/support with gcc, on any host. src/ is not
modified: build.sh copies the sources out and patches them there.

The patches (patches/mdtools/gnu/)
----------------------------------
mdgen-mdlint-host-endian.patch

1. Endianness. MDESC is network byte order and Sun built on SPARC, so their
   hton/ntoh macros are identity and the little-endian arm is an #error. The
   patch adds a real arm keyed on __BYTE_ORDER__, in all three files that
   carry the block.

2. A missing swap. output_bin.c writes an integer property without hton64(),
   while the arc case above it applies one -- a real Sun bug, invisible on
   big-endian, unfixed through the version vendored here. Without it every
   integer property comes out byte-reversed and nothing warns.

mdgen-mdlint-printf-int64.patch

   Prints uint64_t with PRIx64/PRId64 instead of %llx/%lld, so that -Wformat
   is clean on an LP64 host. Cosmetic: the output is unchanged.

build.sh also regenerates mdlex.c with flex and passes -include stdint.h
(md_impl.h relies on Solaris header pull-in order) -- neither is a source
change.

Validation
----------
The MD blobs built with these tools are pinned by hash in
tests/full/md/expected/blobs.sha256 (make md-verify), and the sun path
(Sun's own compiler) must give the same bytes (make sun-verify). Re-check
both if the vendored sources are updated.
